From 6a70ed2d0f6488fbac936b7c261e8a04f8eb53c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approval): Code from External cards offer a source the
 command does not show

A command can fetch and build a repo with no URL in its text: it sources a script and calls a function of it (. scripts/ci/lib.sh; d=$(spirv_val_dir)) that clones and builds. The card then offered no "Allow code from <source> in this chat" button, though the review had named the source in its reason.

The source now comes from the code that runs. The URLs in the functions a sourced script defines and the command calls (and the ones they call) are read from the file on the machine the command runs on, when it is a plain file of at most 200 KB inside a git work tree and the command does not change it. When that finds nothing, the stage-2 review is asked for a <source>host/owner/repo</source> field with a Code from External verdict, and the card offers it only when it is exactly one source on a known forge or package host: no look-alike host, wildcard, variable, list or port.

The grant covers a later call whose script downloads are all granted, or that the review attributes to the same source; a download from another source, a function the command redefines, a dangerous pattern (bash -c) and a command that names another source still ask. URLs in a shell comment of the command no longer count as the command's sources.
